# Copy to .env.local and adjust. .env.local is gitignored.

# Image tag built and run by the launcher.
DEVENV_IMAGE=devenv:local

# Allowlist location. Defaults to allowlist.txt next to the launcher.
#DEVENV_ALLOWLIST_FILE=/absolute/path/to/allowlist.txt

# Git identity for commits made inside the sandbox. Each agent already commits
# as agent-claude / agent-codex / agent-agy without any setting. Use this to
# tell two sessions of the same agent apart: DEVENV_AGENT=claude-review makes
# that session commit as agent-claude-review. Addresses are always local and
# unroutable (@devenv.local).
#DEVENV_AGENT=

# Resource limits. Unset means unlimited, which is the default. The point is
# not to make a session faster but to stop one agent from eating the machine,
# so a second agent - and your own interactive work - stay responsive.
# The numbers below are a starting point for an eight-core machine, not a
# measured optimum. See "Resource limits" in the README before relying on them.

# CPU share - about half of an eight-core machine. Whole numbers are worth
# preferring: Node sizes its worker pools from the quota and floors it, so 2.5
# buys nothing over 2.
#DEVENV_CPUS=4

# Memory ceiling per session.
#DEVENV_MEMORY=8g

# Total of memory plus swap. Left unset it follows DEVENV_MEMORY, which means
# no swap at all - docker's own default would allow the same amount again on
# disk, so 8g would really be a ceiling of 16. Set it higher to allow some
# swap, or -1 for unlimited. It is a total, so it can never be below
# DEVENV_MEMORY. With swap off, overshooting the limit is a SIGKILL rather
# than a slowdown; see "Resource limits" in the README.
#DEVENV_MEMORY_SWAP=12g

# Cap on processes and threads. Generous for a build, but catches a runaway
# install or test runner before it reaches the host.
#DEVENV_PIDS=1024

# Relabel option for bind mounts. Not needed on Docker's default configuration
# even with SELinux enforcing, since docker does not label containers unless it
# is told to. Needed with "selinux-enabled": true in daemon.json, and on
# Podman, where labelling is on by default. Must start with a colon. Empty by
# default, which leaves the mount strings unchanged. That path is untested -
# see "Portability" in the README.
#DEVENV_MOUNT_SUFFIX=:z
